A `graph:` mapping node is a subgraph. Its own row is tagged `*(subgraph)*` and carries its outer
dependencies with its `repeat:` prose as the summary; the rows of its inner steps follow, tagged
`*(in pipeline)*` and carrying inner-scope dependencies. Sections render in outer wave order with
the `## Subgraph:` intro standing in front of its inner `## Step:` sections, and the intro lists
`After:`, `Repeat:` and the inner waves.

The subgraph key `pipeline` is a grouping node with no step directory of its own and is never
reported as a missing step: a healthy subgraph playbook carries no notice line at all.

